<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23569" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-nŏvo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to renew</i>, <i>alter.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plurima innovare instituit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					1, 2, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—So in <i>part. pass.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innŏ-vātus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>renewed</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Min. Fel. Oct. 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. 7, 22 <i>med.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: se ad aliquam rem, <i>to return to a thing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se ad suam intemperantiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 36, 89</span></i>
			.—As a translation of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καινιεῖ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Eccli. 38, 30</span></i>: vox mallei innovat aurem, <i>the noise of the hammer is ever in his ears.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
